{"name":"Cigarette Glow","hex":"#ee5500","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cigarette","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small cigar consisting of tobacco or another substance, wrapped up in a thin roll with paper, intended for smoking."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give someone a cigarette, or to light one for them."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cigarette"},{"term":"glow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit heat and light without a flame.","To emit heat and light without a flame."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of heat and light being emitted by a hot object.","A state of heat being emitted by a person or an animal's body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cigarette","blocks":[{"text":"A cigarette is a thin cylinder of tobacco rolled in thin paper for smoking. Igniting one end causes it to smolder, and the smoker inhales the resulting smoke through the other end. Cigarette smoking is the most common method of tobacco consumption. The term cigarette usually refers to a tobacco cigarette, but the word is sometimes used to refer to other substances, such as a cannabis cigarette or an herbal cigarette. A cigarette differs from a cigar in its smaller size, use of processed leaf, different smoking method, and paper wrapping, which is typically white."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Cigarette_DS.jpg/330px-Cigarette_DS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cigarette","wikidata":"Q1578"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/2015_E-papieros_mod_01.JPG/500px-2015_E-papieros_mod_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/2015_E-papieros_mod_01.JPG/1280px-2015_E-papieros_mod_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikip